# Rosie, no RTC battery: the PMIC's RTC (nvvrs-pseq-rtc, rtc0) is a module that registers
# ~11-13 s into boot and sets the system clock from itself - 1970 - after rosie-clock.service
# has already restored the saved time (2026-09-28 cold boot: restored at 9.3 s, back to
# 1970 at 11.3 s, "nvvrs-pseq-rtc: setting system clock to 1970-01-01T00:00:33 UTC").
# So restore again the moment it appears - through systemd (rosie-clock-rtc.service): run
# directly from this rule it failed, udev's sandbox may not set the clock (2026-09-29).
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="rtc", KERNEL=="rtc0", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="rosie-clock-rtc.service"
